+### 12.3.9 Bounded PEP 621 requirement-string parse failures (R07-C D-M-P)
+
+For `env.llm_critical_deps_pinned` only, extend the internal
+`DeclarationReadIssue` vocabulary with `unparsed_requirement`. This is a captured
+extraction failure, not a declaration that an entire manager document is
+unreadable or that the tool implements every dependency-specifier grammar.
+
+Limit the trigger to string entries actually traversed by the existing
+successfully decoded `pyproject.toml` extractor in two locations:
+`project.dependencies` when its existing value is a list, and each list value
+in an existing mapping `project.optional-dependencies`.
+
+Only an already-caught failure of that entry's existing `Requirement` call
+triggers the new fact. Keep the original parse/diagnostic boundary and caller
+context; do not infer failure from `unparsed` prose, reparse a string or add
+reads. The shared helper's requirements-graph and embedded-pip callers do not
+opt in. Record at most one `unparsed_requirement` per logical source file.
+Preserve any existing `unreadable`, `invalid_syntax` or `invalid_structure` for
+that source instead of replacing it with this cause.
+
+Missing keys, valid empty lists/mappings and skipped non-string members do not
+themselves create this cause; the existing structure checks remain independent.
+An empty or whitespace-only PEP 621 string is included when its existing parse
+call fails; do not coalesce it into absence. Preserve legacy/manual default-empty
+internal failure dictionaries. No persisted schema field is added.
+
+Preserve all partial declarations and order, specifiers, exact versions,
+paths/lines, lock sets and associations, manifest/lock presence, qualified project
+roots, uncertain barriers, scan/read traces, budgets and existing diagnostics.
+Keep successful original parses unchanged, including URLs, markers, extras,
+unversioned requirements, arbitrary equality, ranges and wildcard clauses under
+the existing exact-version contract. Do not repair/split malformed entries,
+strip comments, infer package names or retry with a new grammar. D-C's graph-only
+inline-comment fallback does not extend to these strings.
+
+Reuse §12.3.6's existing declaration-failure consumption, message, fix hint and
+evidence. Exact declarations or qualified lock credit win first, then D-F/D-S,
+then D-L, then the existing nonempty declaration-failure dictionary, then D-G.
+Retain earlier branches' messages/evidence. A new source may add its distinct
+sorted path to an existing D-M finding without changing status. Keep its original
+first declaration/import evidence and file-level failure evidence, not new
+per-entry evidence. Introduce no new rule branch, status or per-package PASS.
+
+Influence remains repository-wide under §12.2's existential exact contract.
+Even an unrelated subproject or empty/whitespace malformed string can
+conservatively make remaining currently used, uncredited critical packages
+SKIPPED/INFO. This cost does not assert an exact pin exists or can be recovered,
+grant credit, infer unknown use or certify complete analysis. Preserve
+no-critical-package applicability and the Python empty-result veto; Python
+coverage does not control this declaration-failure branch.
+
+Keep FAIL-only severity overrides, suppression, ordering and thresholds. An
+isolated WARNING or promoted CRITICAL may stop causing exit 1; an independent
+qualifying finding can still cause exit 1. Default text may show PASS with a
+skipped count. Default export continues to list only WARNING/CRITICAL notable
+findings, so a warning converted to SKIP is no longer listed; complete JSON
+retains the finding. Profile/init consumers retain the same captured inventory.
+No unrelated notable finding is removed.
+
+This slice excludes Poetry/Pipfile package values, environment embedded-pip
+strings, requirements line/directive/include/continuation grammar, new dependency
+groups or dynamic/build extraction, other decoded shapes, unknown/omitted
+use/candidates, listing/README/config/framework completeness and sufficient
+certificates. Do not change engine, scanner, redaction, persisted schemas,
+dependencies, version, historical gold or resource results. Wider R07-C remains
+OPEN.
 
